  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:4891",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have a direct relationship with Thymic stromal lymphopoietin through a series of intermediate targets. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N acts as a target for multiple entities, including Leukocyte common antigen and A704, which in turn target 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid. This compound is known to regulate Thymic stromal lymphopoietin, indicating a potential pathway through which Mollicellin N influences its expression. Additionally, Mollicellin N is linked to TE-9, which targets Patupilone, which also has a target of Thymic stromal lymphopoietin. While the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear, the consistent presence of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid as a common intermediary suggests a shared regulatory role in the signaling pathways leading to Thymic stromal lymphopoietin. The evidence supports a plausible, though not fully elucidated, mechanism by which Mollicellin N may influence Thymic stromal lymphopoietin through these intermediaries.",
